	<Item Name="title" Type="String">Genome-wide CRISPR loss-of-function screen for &#945;-amanitin</Item>
	<Item Name="summary" Type="String">The &#8220;death cap&#8221;, Amanita phalloides, is the world&#8217;s most poisonous mushroom, responsible for 90% of mushroom-related fatalities. The most fatal component of the death cap is &#945;-amanitin(AMA). Despite its lethal effect, the exact mechanisms of how &#945;-amanitin poisons humans remain unclear, leading to no specific antidote available for treatment. Here, we performed a genome-wide CRISPR loss-of-function screen to identify genes and pathways involved in AMA cytotoxicity.</Item>
